<title>USA: AFTER THE BELL - Silent night for stocks.</title>
<headline>AFTER THE BELL - Silent night for stocks.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>After hours trading was very quiet with light volume and little news to move stocks on the Christmas Eve holiday, traders said.</p>
<p>&quot;There's nothing going on,&quot; a trader said.</p>
<p>At the New York Stock Exchange, 10,400 shares were traded after hours. Yesterday, session one volume was 149,900 shares, while session two volume totaled 3,177,600.</p>
